Why Helm? The Problem with Raw YAML
Over Days 1 through 3, you deployed raw YAML files (deployment.yaml, service.yaml, ingress.yaml). In enterprise environments, this creates major challenges:

YAML Sprawl & Duplication: Deploying across dev, staging, and prod usually means copying and
 pasting entire directories of manifests, changing only an image tag, replica count, or environment variable.

No Versioning or Rollbacks: kubectl apply doesn't track revisions of multi-resource applications
 as a single unit. Rolling back a broken multi-service deployment requires manual tracking.

No Package Management: Installing third-party tools (like Prometheus, Redis, or Cert-Manager) would
 require managing dozens of raw upstream manifests yourself.

Helm is the package manager for Kubernetes (think apt, yum, or npm, but for cluster workloads). 
It bundles your YAML manifests into dynamic, parameterized packages called Charts.


